        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "**CT02 \u2014 How damping changes a spring**  \n**How does damping change an oscillation?** Run **8 s at 100 Hz**, then open Scope.  \nm=1 kg, k=4 N/m, b=1 N\u00b7s/m. Initial x=1 m, v=0. Compare each signal in its own units.  \nChange damping factor 1 \u2192 3; rerun. Expect less overshoot. The gain is b/m, not the damping ratio.  \n[Open CT02 student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/CT02-damped-modes/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT teaching materials](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-003-signals-and-systems-fall-2011/resources/mit6_003f11_lec04/) \u00b7 [S7 integrator rules](qrc:/s7studio/help/docs/INTEGRATORS.md)",
          "text_format": "markdown",
          "width": 1374,
          "height": 260,
          "font_size": 18
        }
      }
    ]
